
aifoundry3 - AI Foundry lab machine with 1 ET-SoC-1 card (driver et_soc1 0.20.0)
  card 0  PCI 0000:02:00.0  /dev/et0_mgmt /dev/et0_ops  firmware 1.3.1 (as of 2026-09-25)
  Pinned at every boot to minion 600 MHz / NoC 400 MHz with a 0 W TDP by et-board-clock-guard.service.
  At this pin the firmware's governor makes no thermal step (as of 2026-09-27 it appears latched), so nothing
  slows a hot die.

* Several accounts use this card. Each device node can be open in ONE process at a time.
  Who is using the card: et-who (in scripts: et-who --check)
* Card use is logged (who, which program, when; never arguments or files). Last 24 hours: et-usage
* New here? et-lab-start checks this machine and sets up your account (no sudo);
  the prompt for your coding agent: https://spacesheep.dev/@yaroslavvb/aifoundry-lab-start
* Reserve the card for a run:  flock /run/lock/etsoc-shire0.lock <command>   (CI jobs use this lock)
* These commands change the card for every user: reset, trace level, telemetry stats reset (ettelem --reset-ms),
  temperature thresholds, TDP, frequency, active power management.
* Stop tools and samplers with Ctrl-C or plain kill, never kill -9: a request cut off mid-way leaves a
  stale reply, and the next program that opens the card dies with std::bad_function_call. To clear it once:
  /opt/et/bin/dev_mngt_service -m DM_CMD_GET_MODULE_POWER -n 0 -u 5000
* Vendor tools: /opt/et/bin (on PATH in login shells). Link /opt/et/lib with -Wl,-rpath,/opt/et/lib.
  /opt/et/lib/libetrt.so here is a patched -O3 build (upstream 836a4ab + event-id fix, 2026-07-23);
  aifoundry2 runs the stock 353f20e build.
* Host programs: register the runtime's log levels first in main, or about one launch in 100 crashes at 1.08 s
  (a race in libetrt): see registerRuntimeLogLevels() in github.com/yaroslavvb/et-soc1-prototyping.
* The etsoc1-demo web service (port 5000) can launch jobs on the card.
* /tmp is cleared at every boot: keep your work in your home directory.
* Crash dumps of your programs: coredumpctl list ; coredumpctl gdb <pid>
* Machine facts to record with a measurement: et-lab-manifest.  Health check (read-only): et-lab-health
* Lab accounts and notes: https://spacesheep.dev/@yaroslavvb/aifoundry-lab-accounts
